1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,000
Out past Neptune, cold worlds may be moving in the dark.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,700
SPHEREx maps the whole sky every 6 months in 102 infrared colours.

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,400
Everything near the Sun that moves is in those 65 MB files.

4
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:10,800
Meet MIRA. Point at any place in the sky, play 27 years of NASA images, see what moved, and measure it.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,800
Scrub 27 years: 2MASS, WISE, then SPHEREx.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,300
Measure its motion, read methane in its light, and let an AI model check every field.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,300
17,604 moving stars confirmed. 635 are in no reference database.

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,200
Anyone can help look at one.
